  "latestPeriod": "2026-27 (financial year)",
  "coverage": "Where the Centre's money comes from: taxes (net of the states' share) by type, non-tax revenue, capital receipts, ₹ crore, 1970-71 on",
  "note": "RBI, Central Government receipts, major components (DBIE report 655; Handbook of Statistics on the Indian Economy). Amounts in ₹ crore (DBIE serves rupees). All taxes in this table are net of the states' share (Handbook note 2). GST, from July 2017, is CGST plus IGST plus the GST compensation cess (discontinued from 1 February 2026); it replaced most of the Centre's excise duty and service tax, so excise and GST are read together across 2017-18. Capital receipts exclude the drawdown of cash balances. Stages, from the printed table's own note: accounts to 2024-25, the revised estimate for 2025-26 and the budget estimate for 2026-27, each in its own series (suffix __re and __be), never one line. Cross-checked against the printed table (Innovation Hub export of Handbook report 181): 689 of 693 figures match."
 },
